-- title:
--   Descent of kernel-invariant power series along an isogeny over a field
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a field and $n$ a natural number, and let $F$ and $F'$ be $n$-dimensional formal group laws over $B$: each is an $n$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ whose components have vanishing constant term, whose linear coefficients in each of the two blocks of variables are $\delta_{ij}$, and which satisfy the associativity identity; both are assumed commutative, i.e. each component is unchanged by the substitution interchanging the two blocks of variables. Let $\rho : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ be an $n$-tuple of power series with $\rho_i(0) = 0$ which is a homomorphism from $F$ to $F'$, in the sense that for each $i$ the substitution of $F$ into $\rho_i$ equals the substitution of the pair $(\rho(x),\rho(y))$ into $F'_i$. Assume that there is an $N$ with $x_i^N \in (\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ for all $i$, and that the quotient $B[\![x]\!]/(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ is finite and projective as a $B$-module. The conclusion is that for every $G \in B[\![x]\!]$ such that $G(F(x,y)) - G(x)$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by $\rho_1(y),\dots,\rho_n(y)$, there exists $H \in B[\![x]\!]$ with $G = H(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ and $H(0) = G(0)$.
--
--   This is the descent statement for an isogeny of commutative formal group laws over a field: a power series invariant under translation by the kernel of $\rho$ is a power series in the coordinates of $\rho$, normalised so that the constant terms agree. It is used in the construction over a field of a quasi-inverse to an isogeny of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isODHom_comp_eq_act_pow_of_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_field`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isODHom_comp_eq_act_pow_of_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_field); the hypothesis that the kernel algebra is finite over the base is supplied in that application by the computation of the rank of the kernel of $\varpi$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_eq_subst_of_subst_toPowerSeries_sub_mem_span_of_X_pow_mem_span_of_field.lean

